# The contact form's endpoint, and it must stay above the /* catch-all at the
# bottom: rules are matched in order and the first hit wins, so anything below
# that line is unreachable. The 200! is a rewrite, not a redirect — the browser
# keeps posting to /api/enquiry and never sees the function's real path — and
# the ! forces it to win over the static file that would otherwise be served.
#
# This lives here rather than in netlify.toml, where it was first written and
# silently did nothing: Netlify reads this file *before* netlify.toml, so the
# catch-all below was matching /api/enquiry before the toml was ever consulted.
# Every POST came back as the HTML page with a 200, which is indistinguishable
# from a working form until you notice no email arrived. One file, one order.
/api/enquiry  /.netlify/functions/enquiry  200!

